# #5: the owner-contract step, before and after warming the bridge

The failing step of tests run 42823973007 is step 9 "Validate preamble owner contracts": it runs
sage-extensions' own `tests/lattices/test_lattice_database_owner_contracts.sage` and
`tests/lattices/test_coordinate_diagonal_embeddings.py` from a checkout of that repository's main,
with its own `pyproject.toml` `addopts`, which include `--timeout=60 --timeout-method=signal`.

Reproduced here in the image, with the same command, the same two files, the same inifile and the
same plugins (`-p qc_sage_session -p qc_unique_inventory`), against the sage-extensions copy the
image bakes in at `/repos/sage-extensions` (`7b222e8621`):

    $ run.sh -w /sage-ext ... pytest -p qc_sage_session -p qc_unique_inventory \
        tests/lattices/test_lattice_database_owner_contracts.sage \
        tests/lattices/test_coordinate_diagonal_embeddings.py
    timeout: 60.0s
    collected 13 items
    ======================= 1 warning in 61.17s (0:01:01) =======================
    ! _pytest.outcomes.Exit: ...::test_positive_a2_genus_and_orthogonal_group_are_owned_by_the_lattice:
      Timeout (>60.0s) from pytest-timeout. !
    PYEXIT=1

One test, 61 s, and the run is over: the first contract that reaches the Julia bridge pays the
session start, which the owner records as `61 s` on the first call and `0.0 s` on every later one
(sage-extensions#237). The ceiling is the owner's; this repository does not raise it.

## The change: start the bridge before pytest exists

`results/tests-workflow-warm-owner-bridge.patch` prepends one call to the step's `-c` preamble:

    from sage.all import ZZ; from sage_extensions.categories.lattices import Lattices;
    Lattices(ZZ)([[2, -1], [-1, 2]]).orthogonal_group().order()

That is the owner's own operation, done once outside any test's timer, exactly as a session warm-up
does it. pytest's 60 s ceiling is untouched, the test still computes and asserts its order, and no
assertion changes.

The same invocation with the warm-up:

    against sage-extensions main 38f8109:   1 failed, 12 passed in 6.60s   (contract run, both files)
    against the image's 7b222e8621:         2 failed, 11 passed in 8.91s

So the timeout is gone: thirteen items in seven seconds instead of one item in sixty-one.

## What is still red, and why it is not this repository's

At sage-extensions **main**, the single remaining failure is their own test:

    tests/lattices/test_lattice_database_owner_contracts.sage:148:
        series = lattice.primitive_orbit_series()
    sage_extensions/categories/lattices.py:3305: in primitive_orbit_series
        return primitive_orbit_series(self, bound=bound)
    sage_extensions/categories/lattice_orbit_invariants.py:136:
    E   ValueError: primitive bounded orbit series requires a definite lattice,
        not Integral lattice of rank 5 and signature (2, 3)

That is sage-extensions#286, open: their contract asks an indefinite lattice for its primitive orbit
series and their own code refuses it. The same precondition is what blocks #16 in this repository, so
the contract step cannot be green until #286 lands. Nothing here is narrowed, deselected or skipped
to hide it.

Against the image's baked `7b222e8621` a second owner defect shows as well, and it is green at main:
`test_root_and_theta_catalogue_invariants_are_owned_by_the_lattice` fails with
`AttributeError: 'int' object has no attribute 'parent'` at
`sage_extensions/categories/definite_lattices.py:294`. It is the image's revision, not ours, and not
main.
